    {
      "id": "github_truncated_du_preserves_refused_directory_rows",
      "seq": 530031,
      "targets": [
        "github"
      ],
      "session": "sealed",
      "command": "du /trunc/src 2>/dev/null | grep '/cache$'",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "0\t/trunc/src/cache\n",
        "stderr": ""
      },
      "note": "A truncated GitHub tree uses the generic folder walk: an unreadable subtree keeps its zero-byte directory row and du exits 1, as GNU coreutils 9.7 does."
    },
    {
      "id": "github_submodule_only_directory_is_an_empty_directory",
      "seq": 530032,
      "targets": [
        "github"
      ],
      "command": "du /data/mods; du -a /data/mods; find /data/mods; find /data/mods -empty; ls -A /data/mods; ls -la /data/mods | awk 'NR==1 {print} NR>1 {print $NF}'",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "0\t/data/mods\n0\t/data/mods\n/data/mods\n/data/mods\ntotal ?\n.\n..\n",
        "stderr": ""
      },
      "note": "data-v1's SUBMODULES puts the gitlink mods/lib in a directory that holds nothing else. The tree drops a gitlink, so mods is an empty directory: du keeps its 0 row with and without -a (bytes, as GNU coreutils 9.7 du -b counts it), find names it and calls it -empty as GNU findutils 4.10.0 does, and ls lists only . and .. under the total ls -la cannot know."
    },
    {
      "id": "github_find_mtime_matches_nothing",
      "seq": 530033,
      "targets": [
        "github"
      ],
      "command": "find /repo/docs -mtime -100000; echo rc=$?; find /repo/docs -newermt 2000-01-01 | wc -l",
      "note": "A git tree carries no timestamp, so every entry's mtime is unknown and a time test keeps none of them, on both hosts. GNU find on a checkout would list every file, each with its checkout time.",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "rc=0\n0\n",
        "stderr": ""
      }
    },
